From: Piotr Gorski <lucjan.lucjanov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:11:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zstd: fix DDict hash-set probe index wrap-around

ZSTD_DDictHashSet_emplaceDDict() and ZSTD_DDictHashSet_getDDict() advance their
probe index with:

    idx &= idxRangeMask;
    idx++;

which leaves idx == idxRangeMask + 1 (that is, ddictPtrTableSize) when the probe
starts on the last slot. The loop then re-reads ddictPtrTable[idx] out of range,
and emplaceDDict() writes ddictPtrTable[idx] = ddict one element past the end.
The mask-then-increment spelling never wraps back to zero.

Fold the wrap into the increment instead, so the index is always in range.

This is an extracted subset of a larger zstd dev-tree merge, not an independent
submission: the hunks below are taken verbatim from
sirlucjan-kernel-patches/7.3-rc/zstd-dev-patches/0001-zstd-7.3-merge-v1.6.0-into-kernel-tree.patch
which carries the same change alongside a BMI2 dispatch refactor. That refactor
is deliberately not taken here, because our 2128-2130 series depends on the
existing bmi2 field and would need rebasing onto it.

Reachability is low on this machine: the DDict hash set is only exercised by
multi-dictionary streaming decompression, and zram/zswap use dictionary-less
contexts. Taken because it is a latent out-of-bounds write in vendored code, and
because it will otherwise arrive with the next upstream zstd sync.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Gorski <lucjan.lucjanov@gmail.com>
---

diff --git a/lib/zstd/decompress/zstd_decompress.c b/lib/zstd/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
index bb009554e..fcc5ecb47 100644
--- a/lib/zstd/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
+++ b/lib/zstd/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
@@ -110,8 +110,7 @@ static size_t ZSTD_DDictHashSet_emplaceDDict(ZSTD_DDictHashSet* hashSet, const Z
             hashSet->ddictPtrTable[idx] = ddict;
             return 0;
         }
-        idx &= idxRangeMask;
-        idx++;
+        idx = (idx + 1) & idxRangeMask;
     }
     DEBUGLOG(4, "Final idx after probing for dictID %u is: %zu", dictID, idx);
     hashSet->ddictPtrTable[idx] = ddict;
@@ -158,8 +157,7 @@ static const ZSTD_DDict* ZSTD_DDictHashSet_getDDict(ZSTD_DDictHashSet* hashSet,
             /* currDictID == 0 implies a NULL ddict entry */
             break;
         } else {
-            idx &= idxRangeMask;    /* Goes to start of table when we reach the end */
-            idx++;
+            idx = (idx + 1) & idxRangeMask;    /* Goes to start of table when we reach the end */
         }
     }
     DEBUGLOG(4, "Final idx after probing for dictID %u is: %zu", dictID, idx);
